From d3895a872bedc54b8b642505950111d3d0827603 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sureshkumar <suresure@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 09:25:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [prplmesh] Band steering and MLO reporting fixes

Add support for BTM-only steering mode by allowing steering without ACL-based blocking,
avoiding delays and side effects during soft/idle steering scenarios.

Ensure the serving BSS is always excluded from blocking to maintain client connectivity
and prevent disruption of steering flows.

Fix MLO client LEAVE reporting to use MLD-level identifiers instead of link-level values,
as required by EasyMesh specification.

Correct MLO client reporting in topology data to consistently use AP MLD identifiers,
avoiding reliance on link-level assumptions.

Signed-off-by: Sureshkumar <suresure@qti.qualcomm.com>
